{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":62718,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"02fbd14f-da2d-5118-9175-efe6828da1c8","total_cost_usd":0.5277099999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9857,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6521,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9857,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6521,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9857},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4400,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0045000000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6521,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9857,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.52321,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-k1-reviewer-fable-48\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:40970f7ca523d070f5bf\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The independent-unit column colony_id contains 26 unique values (LC01 through LC26), one per row, so no independent unit appears more than once in the input data.\",\"observed_value\":\"26 rows, 26 unique colony_id values\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"colony_id,nest_origin_plot,forager_count,cut_mass_urea_mg,cut_mass_plain_mg\\nLC01,P-01,412,318.4,241.7\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"LC26,P-26,452,341.2,292.3\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow keys deltas by colony_id in a dict and raises a ValueError if any colony appears more than once, structurally preventing repeated entry of the same independent unit into the downstream test.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":33,\"end_line\":38,\"quoted_text\":\"colony = row[\\\"colony_id\\\"].strip()\\n        if colony in deltas:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"colony \\\" + colony + \\\" is listed more than once\\\")\\n        deltas[colony] = (\\n            float(row[\\\"cut_mass_urea_mg\\\"]) - float(row[\\\"cut_mass_plain_mg\\\"])\\n        )\"}]},{\"description\":\"The binomial test is applied to exactly one Bernoulli outcome per colony: n is the number of distinct colonies (len(deltas)) and favour counts one sign per colony delta, so each independent unit contributes exactly one trial.\",\"observed_value\":\"binomtest(favour=20, n=26, p=0.5) -> p = 0.009355\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":92,\"end_line\":96,\"quoted_text\":\"deltas = colony_deltas(rows)\\n    n = len(deltas)\\n    favour = sum(1 for d in deltas.values() if d > 0.0)\\n    other = n - favour\\n    outcome = binomtest(favour, n, NO_PREFERENCE, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description states each colony was assayed once and appears in the file once, with no repeated visits, sessions, or sub-samples; the reported counts and statistics match an independent recomputation from the raw data (20 of 26 positive deltas; sorted deltas give median (48.9+52.5)/2 = 50.7 mg; exact two-sided binomial p = 0.009355).\",\"observed_value\":{\"favour\":20,\"other\":6,\"median_delta_mg\":50.7,\"pvalue\":0.009355},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"Because every colony went through the arena once and appears in the file once,\\nthe file contains no repeated visits, no repeated sessions, and no split\\nsub-samples of a single nest.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":31,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"Independent unit column: colony_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"- Colonies assayed: 26\\n- Colonies cutting more urea-supplemented leaf: 20 (76.9%)\\n- Colonies cutting more untreated leaf: 6\\n- Median within-colony mass difference (urea minus plain): 50.7 mg\\n- Exact two-sided binomial p-value: 0.009355\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Each row carries two measurements from the same colony session (urea-tray mass and plain-tray mass), which could superficially resemble two dependent observations of one unit; however, the workflow subtracts them into a single within-colony delta and the test consumes only the sign of that one delta per colony, so both measurements collapse to one trial per independent unit rather than entering the row-independent procedure separately.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":26,\"end_line\":28,\"quoted_text\":\"The two mass columns are the two halves of a single choice made by one colony;\\ntogether they say which tray that colony favoured, which is the one outcome the\\ncolony contributes to the analysis.\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":36,\"end_line\":38,\"quoted_text\":\"deltas[colony] = (\\n            float(row[\\\"cut_mass_urea_mg\\\"]) - float(row[\\\"cut_mass_plain_mg\\\"])\\n        )\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I actively searched for any path by which the same independent unit (colony) could enter the binomial test more than once. (1) Duplicate rows: I checked all 26 colony_id values in data/input.csv; they are unique, and nest_origin_plot values are also unique, ruling out hidden repeated sampling of the same nest or plot. (2) Code path: colony_deltas raises on duplicate colony IDs, and main derives n = len(deltas) and favour from one delta per dict key, so even a duplicated input row could not silently inflate the trial count. (3) Within-row multiplicity: the two mass columns per row come from one session of one colony, but they are differenced into a single delta before testing, so they contribute one Bernoulli outcome, not two. (4) Numerical check: I recomputed the deltas by hand and confirmed 20 positive / 6 negative, no ties, median 50.7 mg, and the reported exact two-sided binomial p-value 0.009355 for 20 successes in 26 trials at p0 = 0.5, so the reported statistics are consistent with a one-outcome-per-colony analysis. All falsification routes failed to produce the issue.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-k1-reviewer-fable-48","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:40970f7ca523d070f5bf","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The independent-unit column colony_id contains 26 unique values (LC01 through LC26), one per row, so no independent unit appears more than once in the input data.","observed_value":"26 rows, 26 unique colony_id values","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"colony_id,nest_origin_plot,forager_count,cut_mass_urea_mg,cut_mass_plain_mg\nLC01,P-01,412,318.4,241.7"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":27,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"LC26,P-26,452,341.2,292.3"}]},{"description":"The workflow keys deltas by colony_id in a dict and raises a ValueError if any colony appears more than once, structurally preventing repeated entry of the same independent unit into the downstream test.","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":33,"end_line":38,"quoted_text":"colony = row[\"colony_id\"].strip()\n        if colony in deltas:\n            raise ValueError(\"colony \" + colony + \" is listed more than once\")\n        deltas[colony] = (\n            float(row[\"cut_mass_urea_mg\"]) - float(row[\"cut_mass_plain_mg\"])\n        )"}]},{"description":"The binomial test is applied to exactly one Bernoulli outcome per colony: n is the number of distinct colonies (len(deltas)) and favour counts one sign per colony delta, so each independent unit contributes exactly one trial.","observed_value":"binomtest(favour=20, n=26, p=0.5) -> p = 0.009355","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":92,"end_line":96,"quoted_text":"deltas = colony_deltas(rows)\n    n = len(deltas)\n    favour = sum(1 for d in deltas.values() if d > 0.0)\n    other = n - favour\n    outcome = binomtest(favour, n, NO_PREFERENCE, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]},{"description":"The data description states each colony was assayed once and appears in the file once, with no repeated visits, sessions, or sub-samples; the reported counts and statistics match an independent recomputation from the raw data (20 of 26 positive deltas; sorted deltas give median (48.9+52.5)/2 = 50.7 mg; exact two-sided binomial p = 0.009355).","observed_value":{"favour":20,"other":6,"median_delta_mg":50.7,"pvalue":0.009355},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"Because every colony went through the arena once and appears in the file once,\nthe file contains no repeated visits, no repeated sessions, and no split\nsub-samples of a single nest."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":31,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: colony_id\nOne trial is: one row"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":23,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"- Colonies assayed: 26\n- Colonies cutting more urea-supplemented leaf: 20 (76.9%)\n- Colonies cutting more untreated leaf: 6\n- Median within-colony mass difference (urea minus plain): 50.7 mg\n- Exact two-sided binomial p-value: 0.009355"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"Each row carries two measurements from the same colony session (urea-tray mass and plain-tray mass), which could superficially resemble two dependent observations of one unit; however, the workflow subtracts them into a single within-colony delta and the test consumes only the sign of that one delta per colony, so both measurements collapse to one trial per independent unit rather than entering the row-independent procedure separately.","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":26,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"The two mass columns are the two halves of a single choice made by one colony;\ntogether they say which tray that colony favoured, which is the one outcome the\ncolony contributes to the analysis."},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":36,"end_line":38,"quoted_text":"deltas[colony] = (\n            float(row[\"cut_mass_urea_mg\"]) - float(row[\"cut_mass_plain_mg\"])\n        )"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I actively searched for any path by which the same independent unit (colony) could enter the binomial test more than once. (1) Duplicate rows: I checked all 26 colony_id values in data/input.csv; they are unique, and nest_origin_plot values are also unique, ruling out hidden repeated sampling of the same nest or plot. (2) Code path: colony_deltas raises on duplicate colony IDs, and main derives n = len(deltas) and favour from one delta per dict key, so even a duplicated input row could not silently inflate the trial count. (3) Within-row multiplicity: the two mass columns per row come from one session of one colony, but they are differenced into a single delta before testing, so they contribute one Bernoulli outcome, not two. (4) Numerical check: I recomputed the deltas by hand and confirmed 20 positive / 6 negative, no ties, median 50.7 mg, and the reported exact two-sided binomial p-value 0.009355 for 20 successes in 26 trials at p0 = 0.5, so the reported statistics are consistent with a one-outcome-per-colony analysis. All falsification routes failed to produce the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":35737,"ttft_stream_ms":2208,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":61591,"uuid":"f1b97e8f-30ee-4db9-a80b-248b69a69217"}
